## Scenes

dialogue-farewell-1 = Brookhollow, a wheat village on the southern border of Halvaren. The year 965.
dialogue-farewell-2 = Did you pack everything? Bread, the cloak, the waterskin... let me check again.
dialogue-farewell-3 = I checked twice, Mom. Don’t worry.
dialogue-farewell-4 = Tauryen! I put aside some potions the peddler left. Nobody grows food for you on the road, boy.
dialogue-farewell-5 = Thank you, Granny Hilda. When I’m back, I’ll help you harvest the whole garden.
dialogue-farewell-6 = So it’s really today. You’re going after that being-the-strongest thing?
dialogue-farewell-7 = I am. I’m going to be the strongest adventurer in the whole world.
dialogue-farewell-8 = I know. You’ve said it since we were kids. Go without worrying: I’ll look after your mom and the house until you’re back.
dialogue-farewell-9 = I know you will, Jory. I promise I’ll come back, and this house won’t go short again.
dialogue-farewell-10 = Come back in one piece, son. That’s all I ask.
dialogue-farewell-11 = Tauryen takes the north road, toward Valcrest.

dialogue-brenna-later-1 = Valcrest is past Burrowood, up the north road. Stay on the road, all right?

dialogue-hilda-later-1 = Still here? Take one more carrot, then. For the road.

dialogue-jory-later-1 = The north road won’t walk itself. Go on, I’ve got things covered here.

dialogue-meet-lyra-1 = Shouts and the snap of a bowstring. In the middle of the clearing, a young woman is surrounded by goblins.
dialogue-meet-lyra-2 = One more step and the next one gets an arrow in the eye!
dialogue-meet-lyra-3 = Hold on! I’m coming!
dialogue-meet-lyra-4 = Who are you?! Never mind. If you know how to use that sword, use it!

dialogue-lyra-recon-1 = ...Thanks. I’d have handled it, but... really, thank you.
dialogue-lyra-recon-2 = I’m Tauryen, from Brookhollow. I’m heading to Valcrest to join the Adventurers’ Guild.
dialogue-lyra-recon-3 = Lyra, soldier of the Halvaren army, from Valcrest. I came to scout a goblin camp near here.
dialogue-lyra-recon-4 = Alone?
dialogue-lyra-recon-5 = Alone. It’s my first real mission, and I wasn’t going to ask for a babysitter.
dialogue-lyra-recon-6 = The camp is west of the road. I’m finishing the scouting, with or without you.
dialogue-lyra-recon-7 = With, then. If there are goblins near the road, anyone who travels it is in danger.
dialogue-lyra-recon-8 = ...Fine. Just don’t get in my way.

dialogue-camp-after-1 = The hobgoblin falls, and the goblins left flee into the woods.
dialogue-camp-after-2 = Camp destroyed. That went well past a scouting run... the sergeant will have plenty to say.
dialogue-camp-after-3 = That you did great?
dialogue-camp-after-4 = That I went alone. Come on. Valcrest is north, and I have a report to deliver.

dialogue-the-report-1 = At the army post, a sergeant looks up from his papers.
dialogue-the-report-2 = Soldier Lyra. Report.
dialogue-the-report-3 = Scouting complete, sir. A goblin camp west of the Burrowood road, a hobgoblin in command. The camp has been destroyed.
dialogue-the-report-4 = Destroyed. By whom?
dialogue-the-report-5 = By me and by him, sir. Tauryen, from Brookhollow. He got me out of an ambush.
dialogue-the-report-6 = An ambush. So you went alone.
dialogue-the-report-7 = ...I did, sir.
dialogue-the-report-8 = I ordered a scouting run, not a heroics act. If this young man hadn’t been on that road, I’d be writing a very different report today. Understood?
dialogue-the-report-9 = Understood, sir. I apologize.
dialogue-the-report-10 = ...The report is well done. Dismissed.
dialogue-the-report-11 = And you, Tauryen of Brookhollow. Thank you for bringing my soldier back.
dialogue-the-report-12 = She’s the one who got me through Burrowood. I just showed up at the right time.
dialogue-the-report-13 = You’re going to the Guild, right? It’s past the plaza. ...Thank you, Tauryen. I mean it.
dialogue-the-report-14 = Lyra returns to her post. Tauryen goes on alone.

dialogue-garrick-later-1 = Soldier Lyra is on duty. If you go looking for trouble, adventurer, don’t do it alone.

dialogue-guild-register-1 = The Adventurers’ Guild hall is packed: mugs, maps, veterans bragging.
dialogue-guild-register-2 = Welcome to the Guild! Signing up? Have a seat, it’s quick.
dialogue-guild-register-3 = Name?
dialogue-guild-register-4 = Tauryen, from Brookhollow.
dialogue-guild-register-5 = Here’s how it works: you sign, get your insignia and take missions from the board. You can only accept missions of your own rank or below, all right? No rookies hunting dragons.
dialogue-guild-register-6 = And this waiver says the Guild takes no responsibility for your life. Sign at the bottom.
dialogue-guild-register-7 = Tauryen signs without hesitating.
dialogue-guild-register-8 = Last question, just procedure: what is your goal as an adventurer?
dialogue-guild-register-9 = To be the strongest adventurer in the whole world!
dialogue-guild-register-10 = The whole hall hears it. A moment of silence. Then laughter from wall to wall.
dialogue-guild-register-11 = The strongest in the world! Did you hear that? Start with the sewer rats, champ!
dialogue-guild-register-12 = Delia doesn’t laugh. She looks at Tauryen a little longer than she needs to.
dialogue-guild-register-13 = ...Bronze insignia. Welcome, Tauryen. Good luck.

dialogue-wounded-1 = Nobody wants to team up with the rookie. Before Tauryen reaches the mission board, the door bursts open.
dialogue-wounded-2 = Help!
dialogue-wounded-3 = Two wounded adventurers stumble in carrying a third, unconscious. The laughter turns to silence.
dialogue-wounded-4 = Healers, quick! Brann, Sylas, what happened?
dialogue-wounded-5 = The Golden Blades in this state? What could do that in a remote town like this?
dialogue-wounded-6 = The sewer. We were on patrol, levels 1 and 2, routine... and walked into a Ghoul ambush.
dialogue-wounded-7 = There were rookies down on the floor. The Ghouls were... eating them.
dialogue-wounded-8 = Ghouls in the sewer? That’s Gold-rank stuff!
dialogue-wounded-9 = I held most of them off myself. We were winning, until Fennick took a blow to the head, from behind. A Lich.
dialogue-wounded-10 = A Lich? That’s Platinum...
dialogue-wounded-11 = We finished the Ghouls and wounded the wretch. It’s weak. But with Fennick down, we couldn’t go on.
dialogue-wounded-12 = If that wounded Lich reaches the surface, the whole town is in danger. I’m going down to the sewer.
dialogue-wounded-13 = You hear that? The strongest in the world is off to hunt the Lich!
dialogue-wounded-14 = Nobody takes Tauryen seriously. He walks out the door.
dialogue-wounded-15 = Delia follows Tauryen with her eyes. Then she climbs the stairs to the upper floor.

dialogue-sewer-squad-1 = Footsteps echo down the tunnel. Three army soldiers appear with torches.
dialogue-sewer-squad-2 = Halt! Civilian, what are you doing here? The army takes it from here. Leave the sewer.
dialogue-sewer-squad-3 = ...Tauryen?
dialogue-sewer-squad-4 = Lyra! I can help.
dialogue-sewer-squad-5 = You’re a civilian. Leave now, or I’ll arrest you.
dialogue-sewer-squad-6 = I’m not a civilian. I’m with the Adventurers’ Guild, and Guild members can take missions in its name.
dialogue-sewer-squad-7 = Tauryen shows his Bronze insignia.
dialogue-sewer-squad-8 = Missions of your own rank or below, rookie. Hunting a Lich is a Platinum-rank mission.
dialogue-sewer-squad-9 = I didn’t say anything about hunting a Lich. I came to hunt the sewer rats.
dialogue-sewer-squad-10 = Tauryen shows the mission sheet he took from the Guild board: "Kill 20 rats". Bronze rank.
dialogue-sewer-squad-11 = ...That’s...
dialogue-sewer-squad-12 = But I can’t leave the people of this town in danger, either. I’ll do my best to find out where the wounded Lich went.
dialogue-sewer-squad-13 = Wounded? The Lich is wounded?!
dialogue-sewer-squad-14 = That’s what the Golden Blades said at the Guild. They wounded it before they fled.
dialogue-sewer-squad-15 = Corporal, I know Tauryen. He saved me at the goblin camp. He can look after himself.
dialogue-sewer-squad-16 = ...A wounded Lich changes everything. Very well, adventurer. You’re with us, but you follow orders. Tobin, Lyra, form up.
dialogue-sewer-squad-17 = Yes, sir!

dialogue-delia-board-1 = Meanwhile, at the Guild...
dialogue-delia-board-2 = Delia walks past the mission board. One sheet is missing: "Kill 20 rats".
dialogue-delia-board-3 = ...So that’s what you did, rookie.
dialogue-delia-board-4 = She smiles.

dialogue-clue-slime-1 = On the tunnel floor, a trail of cold black slime, like wet ash.
dialogue-clue-slime-2 = That’s no rat. That’s undead blood.
dialogue-clue-slime-3 = It leads toward the torn grate.

dialogue-clue-grate-1 = An iron grate torn out of the wall. Past it, the trail goes down to level 2.
dialogue-clue-grate-2 = It came through here. It’s going down.
dialogue-clue-grate-3 = The stairs to level 2 are right there. It gets harder from here. Stay sharp, all of you.

dialogue-lich-appears-1 = At the end of the tunnel, the wall lies in ruins. Beyond it, a vast hall, older than the sewer.
dialogue-lich-appears-2 = A double door at the far end... and a corridor to the left.
dialogue-lich-appears-3 = Let’s check the door. Slowly.
dialogue-lich-appears-4 = A chill cuts through the hall. Out of the corridor comes a figure in torn robes, its clawed hand wrapped in shadow.
dialogue-lich-appears-5 = The Lich! Form up!
dialogue-lich-appears-6 = It’s wounded. Together, we can do this!

dialogue-lich-final-1 = The Lich collapses... and, with its last thread of mana, rises again, its claw aimed at Tauryen.
dialogue-lich-final-2 = A blade cuts the air. Three adventurers leap through the broken wall, and the Lich crumbles to dust.
dialogue-lich-final-3 = We made it in time. Is everyone in one piece?
dialogue-lich-final-4 = In one piece, thanks to you. Who are you?
dialogue-lich-final-5 = Friends of Delia’s. She asked us to come after a rookie who went down alone.
dialogue-lich-final-6 = You’re Tauryen? Do you know what you did today? You went after a Lich at your level.
dialogue-lich-final-7 = Even with people in danger, you’d have been just one more target. And every extra target makes the mission harder for everyone.
dialogue-lich-final-8 = He’s right. Courage without strength puts others at risk too.
dialogue-lich-final-9 = ...You’re right. I promise I won’t do that again.
dialogue-lich-final-10 = I’ll get stronger. Truly strong, so I can help when something like this happens again.
dialogue-lich-final-11 = Then see that you keep it.
dialogue-lich-final-12 = Heavy footsteps behind the broken wall. Soldiers come in with torches, led by a familiar face.
dialogue-lich-final-13 = Lyra? Corporal Merrick? What happened here?
dialogue-lich-final-14 = A wounded Lich, sir. Defeated, with the Guild’s help.
dialogue-lich-final-15 = ...Understood. The army takes over from here. Everyone out; this place is sealed off.
dialogue-lich-final-16 = The team climbs back to the surface. In the plaza, each goes their own way.
dialogue-lich-final-17 = See you around, Tauryen. And careful with those promises: you’re the kind who keeps them.
dialogue-lich-final-18 = I am. See you, Lyra.
dialogue-lich-final-19 = To be continued...

dialogue-delia-later-1 = Missions are on the board right next door. Remember: your rank or below!
